We are given \(A\) as a rotation by \(\frac{2\pi}{5}\) and \(B\) as a reflection across the x-axis.

\(A\) has order 5 because \(5 \cdot \frac{2\pi}{5} = 2\pi\).  
\(B^2 = I\).  

Check the dihedral relation:  
\(BAB = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix} 
\begin{pmatrix} \cos\frac{2\pi}{5} & -\sin\frac{2\pi}{5} \\ \sin\frac{2\pi}{5} & \cos\frac{2\pi}{5} \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} \cos\frac{2\pi}{5} & \sin\frac{2\pi}{5} \\ -\sin\frac{2\pi}{5} & \cos\frac{2\pi}{5} \end{pmatrix}
= A^{-1}.\)  

So the set of all products is the dihedral group \(D_5\), which has order \(2 \cdot 5 = 10\).

Final answer: 10

